{
  "slug": "claude-code-workflow",
  "name": "Claude Code Workflow",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Six focused slash commands for safer, more deliberate coding sessions. Save and restore named git checkpoints, review diffs before committing, analyze blast radius before changing code, run targeted tests against changed files, and orient quickly in any codebase — all without leaving the Claude Code CLI.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **6 skills**.\n\n- **Skills** (6): `checkpoint` (Create a named git checkpoint (lightweight tag) to save your current state during a session), `context` (Quick project orientation — summarize the stack, structure, and key patterns for a new session), `diff-review` (Self-review uncommitted changes before committing — check for bugs, edge cases, and missing tests), `rollback` (Roll back to a previous checkpoint created by /checkpoint), `scope` (Analyze the blast radius of changing a function, class, or file before modifying it), `verify` (Run relevant tests, type checks, and linters for files changed in the current session)\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install claude-code-workflow@claude-community` from `UtkarshJain98/claude-code-workflow`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude",
    "copilot",
    "antigravity",
    "codex"
  ],
